Article 16. Termination of provision of legal aid services by legal aid-participating organizations

1. Organizations signing contracts to provide legal aid services shall terminate their provisions of legal aid services in the following cases:

a) Have no longer satisfied one of the conditions for signature of contracts for provision of legal aid services as prescribed in clause 2 Article 14 hereof;

b) Terminate the provision of legal aid services under the contract;

c) Cause serious consequences when providing legal aid services;

d) Have their operation terminated in accordance with law.

2. An organization registering for participation in the provision of legal aid services shall terminate its provision of legal aid services in the following cases:
a) Has no longer satisfied one of the conditions for registering for participation in the provision of legal aid services as prescribed in clause 1 Article 15 hereof;

b) It terminates its participation in legal aid services itself after sending a written notification to the provincial Department of Justice that has granted its license for operation registration;
c) It has not provided legal aid services for 02 consecutive years except for cases due to objective reasons;

d) It has caused serious consequences when providing legal aid services;
dd) It has its operation terminated in accordance with law.

3. When terminating provision of legal aid services, the legal aid-participating organization shall send a written notification to the Department of Justice and transfer dossiers of legal aid-related cases that it has not finished to the state legal aid center assigned by the Department of Justice for continuation in handling.

